During the financial year 2015-16, HUDCO has decided to exit from joint venture companies by invoking the exit clauses, as the performance of these joint ventures was not found to be satisfactory. The Company is in the process of exiting from these joint ventures.

In the case of IBHL, an associate Company, HUDCO has invested ₹ 2.50 crore, being 25% of the paid up equity share capital of the investee Company. The investment in HUDCO books is appearing at ₹ 1 only.

